---
description: Keep TypeScript type declarations cohesive and colocated
globs: **/*.ts,**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---
# Type Organization

- Move a cohesive, substantial group of types or interfaces to a colocated
  `*.types.ts` file when declarations dominate or obscure the implementation.
- Keep small, implementation-specific types local when extraction would reduce
  readability.
- Export only the minimal type surface consumers need; keep supporting aliases
  private.
- Use `import type` and `export type` for type-only dependencies.
- Name type modules for their clear owner, such as `block.types.ts`. Do not
  create vague global, shared, or common type dumping grounds.
- Do not use `global.d.ts` for ordinary project types.
- Do not extract types when doing so creates a circular dependency or weakens
  type safety.

```typescript
// BAD: src/types/common.types.ts
export type Data = Record<string, unknown>;

// GOOD: src/block.types.ts
type ColumnMap = Record<string, readonly string[]>;
export type PackedFindingColumns = ColumnMap & { rowCount: number };
```
